endent Andrea James. Polling throughout 2026 has been remarkably stable, with Healey leading by 16 to 24 points in surveys from UNH, MassINC, UMass Amherst and Suffolk. The most recent polls in late September show her ahead by roughly 16 to 21 points among likely voters.\n\nMinogue has tried to make the race about affordability and accountability, while Healey has tied him to President Trump. The Boston Globe reports that Minogue's pitch is not landing, even as the economy remains Healey's softest issue. All seven major raters call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets put Healey's chances around 95 percent. Both sides have spent heavily, about $13 million combined, but the fundamentals point to a comfortable Healey re-election.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9961, "margin": 18.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9947, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9875, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9921, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9953, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9924, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9932, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9949, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9955, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 18.5}]}